  slide "AIPerf: inside one worker process" {
    eyebrow: "AIPerf architecture"
    title: "One event loop, one lightweight task per in-flight credit"
    lede: "A worker doesn't throttle itself — no internal limit on how much it runs at once. Every credit it receives becomes an independent task on its one event loop, sharing one pooled HTTP connection. Concurrency admission happens entirely upstream, at credit issuance."

    narration: "Inside a single worker process, receiving a credit schedules an independent lightweight task on that process's one event loop, tracked in a simple lookup keyed by credit identity. There's no internal limit inside the worker capping how many of these run at once — the worker will happily run however many tasks it's been handed. The actual outbound HTTP calls share one pooled connection manager, sized generously — in the thousands — so it's essentially never the constraint. A worker's own code makes no admission decisions at all; every constraint on how much is running at once was already applied upstream, at the moment the timing/dispatch process decided whether a credit could be issued in the first place. Whatever a worker is handed, it runs — which is exactly why the credit ledger, not the worker, is where AIPerf's concurrency guarantee actually lives."

    term: {
      word: "task-per-credit"
      meaning: "AIPerf's worker concurrency model: every received credit becomes its own lightweight task on the worker's single event loop, with no internal limit — the worker executes whatever concurrency it's handed, because admission was already decided upstream by the credit ledger."
    }

    points: [
      "A received credit becomes an independent task on the worker's one event loop — no worker-side limit.",
      "Outbound HTTP calls share one pooled connection manager, sized generously, rarely the bottleneck.",
      "The worker makes zero admission decisions — it runs exactly whatever concurrency it's been handed.",
      "Real concurrency enforcement lives entirely upstream, at slot acquisition before a credit is ever sent."
    ]

    caption: "The worker doesn't gate anything — the ledger already did."

    render: @scene {
      sdk.Header(
        id = "s10-hdr",
        title = "WORKER: NO SELF-THROTTLING",
        caption = "The worker doesn't gate anything — the ledger already did.",
