  slide "Side by side" {
    eyebrow: "Side by side"
    title: "Where the two architectures actually diverge"
    lede: "Both reach exact steady-state concurrency. Locust does it structurally, one green thread per user with a zero-delay loop; AIPerf does it with an explicit credit ledger a worker never even sees the gating logic for. The ledger is also what makes AIPerf's stop-at-N exact where Locust's is necessarily poll-then-kill."

    narration: "Tracing both down to how they actually work lands on one real divergence, not several. Locust's concurrency is exact once you account for zero think-time and simultaneous user spawn — N green threads, each with at most one in-flight request, is a structural guarantee of the loop itself, no coordinator required. AIPerf's concurrency is exact too, but for a different reason: a slot is explicitly acquired before every dispatch, and the worker that eventually runs the request never makes an admission decision at all. That difference is invisible until you need to stop at an exact total count. Locust has no counter a stop condition could check against — its periodic stats report only fires every few seconds, so stopping at N is necessarily poll, then terminate every green thread, in-flight work included. AIPerf's stop condition reads the exact same counter the credit ledger already maintains, so it can gate the cutoff synchronously and then genuinely drain, waiting on a signal that fires exactly when the last credit returns. AIPerf can also deliberately disable that advantage — its overshoot mode reproduces Locust's poll-then-kill on purpose, for direct comparison, which took bypassing two independent internal limits to pull off cleanly."

    term: {
      word: "the actual divergence"
      meaning: "Not 'exact vs approximate concurrency' — both are exact in steady state. The real difference is whether a central, checkable counter exists at all: AIPerf's credit ledger is that counter, and its existence is what makes an exact stop-at-N gate and a real drain possible; Locust's loop structure gives it exact concurrency without ever needing such a counter, which is exactly why it has none to check for stopping."
    }

    points: [
      "Locust: zero think-time, N users spawned at once → exactly N in flight, self-limiting, no coordinator.",
      "AIPerf: a slot is acquired per dispatch; the worker that runs the request makes no admission decision.",
      "Locust's stop-at-N has nothing to check but a periodic report → poll-then-terminate, no drain by default.",
      "AIPerf's stop-at-N reads the same counter the ledger already maintains → exact gate plus a real drain."
    ]

    caption: "Same steady-state concurrency; the ledger is what makes the cutoff exact."

    render: @scene {
      sdk.Header(
        id = "s11-hdr",
        title = "THE COUNTER IS THE DIFFERENCE",
        caption = "Same steady-state concurrency; the ledger is what makes the cutoff exact.",
        x = 18, y = 16, width = 664, height = 44,
        surfaceRole = theme(surface.secondary),
        inkRole = theme(ink.secondary)
      )
      sdk.Panel(
        id = "s11-locust",
        title = "Locust",
        detail = "exact via loop structure · no counter",
        x = 40, y = 100, width = 280, height = 100,
        surfaceRole = theme(surface.elevated),
        strokeRole = theme(accent.secondary)
      )
      sdk.Panel(
        id = "s11-aiperf",
        title = "AIPerf",
        detail = "exact via credit ledger · has a counter",
        x = 380, y = 100, width = 280, height = 100,
        surfaceRole = theme(surface.elevated),
        strokeRole = theme(accent.primary)
      )
      sdk.Divider(
        id = "s11-div",
        axis = "y",
        x = 350, y = 90, length = 160,
        strokeRole = theme(ink.tertiary)
      )
      sdk.Panel(
        id = "s11-stop-l",
        title = "Stop at N",
        detail = "poll every few seconds, then kill",
        x = 60, y = 240, width = 240, height = 70,
        surfaceRole = theme(surface.elevated),
        strokeRole = theme(accent.warning)
      )
      sdk.Panel(
        id = "s11-stop-a",
        title = "Stop at N",
        detail = "synchronous gate, real drain",
        x = 400, y = 240, width = 240, height = 70,
        surfaceRole = theme(surface.elevated),
        strokeRole = theme(accent.green)
      )
      sdk.Edge(
        id = "s11-e1",
        mode = "route",
        from = { nodeId: "s11-locust", anchor: "s" },
        to = { nodeId: "s11-stop-l", anchor: "n" },
        style = { stroke: theme(accent.warning), strokeWidth: 2 }
      )
      sdk.Edge(
        id = "s11-e2",
        mode = "route",
        from = { nodeId: "s11-aiperf", anchor: "s" },
        to = { nodeId: "s11-stop-a", anchor: "n" },
        style = { stroke: theme(accent.green), strokeWidth: 2 }
      )
      sdk.Signal(
        id = "s11-motion",
        from = { nodeId: "s11-locust", anchor: "center" },
        to = { nodeId: "s11-aiperf", anchor: "center" },
        opacity = 0.45,
        strokeWidth = 2.2,
        label = "the counter is the difference",
        style = { stroke: theme(accent.tertiary) }
      )

      timeline main {
        at 0 reveal s11-hdr duration 260
        after s11-hdr reveal s11-locust duration 280
        after s11-locust reveal s11-div duration 220
        after s11-div reveal s11-aiperf duration 280
        after s11-aiperf trace s11-e1 duration 260
        after s11-e1 reveal s11-stop-l duration 260
        after s11-aiperf trace s11-e2 duration 260
        after s11-e2 reveal s11-stop-a duration 260
        after s11-stop-a trace s11-motion duration 900
      }
    }
  }
}
